{"title": "Sectional Mock #36 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Sonali applied for a job of Science teacher in a school. In the test for job, she scored 8 in Physics, 8 in Chemistry, 6 in Biology, and 6.5 in the interview. For calculating the final score, weightage of 2, 3, 3, and 4 were assigned to Physics, Chemistry, Biology, and interview, respectively. What is the weighted average score of Sonali?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2380;&#2325;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2344;&#2380;&#2325;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2380;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 8, &#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 8, &#2332;&#2368;&#2357; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 6 &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 6.5 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2349;&#2380;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368;, &#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344;, &#2332;&#2368;&#2357; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2, 3, 3 &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366; (&#2357;&#2375;&#2335;&#2375;&#2332;) &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["7", "8.4", "7.2", "21"], "options_hi": ["7", "8.4", "7.2", "21"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total weighted score of Sonali = 8 * 2 + 8 * 3 + 6 * 3 + 6.5 * 4 = 16 + 24 + 18 + 26 = 84</p><p>Total weight = 2 + 3 + 3 + 4 = 12</p><p>Required weighted average = 84/12</p><p>= 7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total weighted score of Sonali = 8 * 2 + 8 * 3 + 6 * 3 + 6.5 * 4 = 16 + 24 + 18 + 26 = 84</p><p>Total weight = 2 + 3 + 3 + 4 = 12</p><p>Required weighted average = 84/12</p><p>= 7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>On the occasion of Republic Day, a retail store offers a scheme where customers can avail a discount of 26% on their total purchase. If Manish buys items worth &#8377; 2,050, how much money (in &#8377;) will he save through the scheme discount</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2339;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2357;&#2360;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2361;&#2340; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342; &#2346;&#2352; 26% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2313;&#2336;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2344;&#2368;&#2359; 2,050 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2348;&#2330;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;</p>", "options_en": ["533", "544", "522", "511"], "options_hi": ["533", "544", "522", "511"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Discount = 26% of 2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  (2000 + 50)</p><p>= (0.26  X  2000) + (0.26  X  50)</p><p>= 520 + 13 = 533</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Discount = 26% of 2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  (2000 + 50)</p><p>= (0.26  X  2000) + (0.26  X  50)</p><p>= 520 + 13 = 533</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If tanA + cotA = 2, then the value of tan<sup>2</sup> A + cot<sup>2</sup> A is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; tanA + cotA = 2, &#2340;&#2379; tan<sup>2</sup> A + cot<sup>2</sup> A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["16", "2", "8", "4"], "options_hi": ["16", "2", "8", "4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here, tanA + cotA = 2</p><p>So tanA + 1/tanA = 2</p><p>tan<sup>2</sup>A + 1 = 2tanA</p><p>tan<sup>2</sup>A  -  2tanA + 1 =0</p><p>(tanA  -  1 )<sup>2</sup>=0</p><p>tanA = 1</p><p>So, cotA =1</p><p>Now putting the values in tan<sup>2</sup> A + cot<sup>2</sup> A ;we have</p><p>1<sup>2</sup> + 1<sup>2</sup> = 2</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, tanA + cotA = 2</p><p>So tanA + 1/tanA = 2</p><p>tan<sup>2</sup>A + 1 = 2tanA</p><p>tan<sup>2</sup>A  -  2tanA + 1 =0</p><p>(tanA  -  1 )<sup>2</sup>=0</p><p>tanA = 1</p><p>So, cotA =1</p><p>Now putting the values in tan<sup>2</sup> A + cot<sup>2</sup> A ;we have</p><p>1<sup>2</sup> + 1<sup>2</sup> = 2</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>The simplification of 5.3<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">2", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; 87 &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2340;&#2350; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["77/18", "79/18", "73/18", "71/18"], "options_hi": ["87", "85", "88", "86"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify: &radic;(7 + 4&radic;3) + &radic;(7 &#8722; 4&radic;3)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;: &radic;(7 + 4&radic;3) + &radic;(7 &#8722; 4&radic;3)</p>", "options_en": ["2", "3", "4", "5"], "options_hi": ["2", "3", "4", "5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>7 &#177; 4&radic;3 = (&radic;3 &#177; 2)&#178;</p><p>&radic;(7 + 4&radic;3) = &radic;3 + 2</p><p>&radic;(7 &#8722; 4&radic;3) = 2 &#8722; &radic;3</p><p>Sum = (&radic;3 + 2) + (2 &#8722; &radic;3) = 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>7 &#177; 4&radic;3 = (&radic;3 &#177; 2)&#178;</p><p>&radic;(7 + 4&radic;3) = &radic;3 + 2</p><p>&radic;(7 &#8722; 4&radic;3) = 2 &#8722; &radic;3</p><p>Sum = (&radic;3 + 2) + (2 &#8722; &radic;3) = 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three successive discounts of 20%, 25% and 5% given on the marked price of an item. What is equivalent discount % given on the item?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 20%, 25% &#2324;&#2352; 5% &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; % &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["41%", "42%", "43%", "44%"], "options_hi": ["41%", "42%", "43%", "44%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Single equivalent discount for successive discount 20% and 25%</p><p>= 20 + 25  -  (20 * 25)/100</p><p>= 40%</p><p>And, single equivalent discount for 40% and 5%</p><p>= 40 + 5  -  (40 * 5)/100</p><p>= <b>43%</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Single equivalent discount for successive discount 20% and 25%</p><p>= 20 + 25  -  (20 * 25)/100</p><p>= 40%</p><p>And, single equivalent discount for 40% and 5%</p><p>= 40 + 5  -  (40 * 5)/100</p><p>= <b>43%</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>HCF and LCM of two numbers are 21 and 2457 respectively. If one number lies between 170 to 200, then the number is : </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 21 &#2324;&#2352; 2457 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 170 &#2360;&#2375; 200 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;: </p>", "options_en": ["183", "175", "199", "189"], "options_hi": ["183", "175", "199", "189"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers are 21a and 21b </p><p>LCM * HCF = product of two numbers</p><p>21 * 2457 = 21a * 21b</p><p>ab = (21 * 2457)/(21 * 21)</p><p>ab = 117</p><p>Two co- prime numbers with product 117 are 13 and 9</p><p>Therefore, the required number is (21 * 13, 21 * 9) = 273 and 189</p><p>Number which lies between 170 to 200 = 189</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers are 21a and 21b </p><p>LCM * HCF = product of two numbers</p><p>21 * 2457 = 21a * 21b</p><p>ab = (21 * 2457)/(21 * 21)</p><p>ab = 117</p><p>Two co- prime numbers with product 117 are 13 and 9</p><p>Therefore, the required number is (21 * 13, 21 * 9) = 273 and 189</p><p>Number which lies between 170 to 200 = 189</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cistern is filled with water by taps A and B together in 42 minutes. If tap B was stopped after 18 min, the cistern is filled in 45 min. The cistern can alone be filled by tap B in:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2344;&#2354; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 42 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2344;&#2354; B &#2325;&#2379; 18 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; 45 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2344;&#2354; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["378 min", "369 min", "360 min", "387 min"], "options_hi": ["378 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "369 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "360 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "387 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let total capacity of cistern = 42 units</p><p>Efficiency of taps A and B together = 42/42 = 1 unit per min</p><p>Part of cistern filled by A and B together in 18 min = 18 * 1 = 18 units</p><p>Remaining capacity of cistern = 42  -  18 = 24 units</p><p>These 24 units is filled by tap A in 45  -  18 = 27 min.</p><p>Efficiency of tap A = 24/27 = 8/9 units per min </p><p>Efficiency of tap B = 1  -  (8/9) = 1/9 units per min</p><p>Time taken by B alone to fill the cistern = 42/ (1/9) = 378 min.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let total capacity of cistern = 42 units</p><p>Efficiency of taps A and B together = 42/42 = 1 unit per min</p><p>Part of cistern filled by A and B together in 18 min = 18 * 1 = 18 units</p><p>Remaining capacity of cistern = 42  -  18 = 24 units</p><p>These 24 units is filled by tap A in 45  -  18 = 27 min.</p><p>Efficiency of tap A = 24/27 = 8/9 units per min </p><p>Efficiency of tap B = 1  -  (8/9) = 1/9 units per min</p><p>Time taken by B alone to fill the cistern = 42/ (1/9) = 378 min.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum of roots of the equation 4x<sup>2</sup>  -  mx + n = 0 is 20, if one root of the equation is 7/2, then find the value of 'n'.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; 4x<sup>2</sup> - mx + n = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 20 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; 7/2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'n' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["241", "231", "181", "251"], "options_hi": ["241", "231", "181", "251"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of roots of the equation = 20</p><p>m/4=20</p><p>m = 80</p><p>One root of the equation = 7/2</p><p>Now,</p><p>4x<sup>2</sup>  -  mx + n = 0</p><p>4*(7/2)<sup>2</sup>  -  80*7/2 + n = 0</p><p>49  -  280 + n = 0</p><p>n = 231</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of roots of the equation = 20</p><p>m/4=20</p><p>m = 80</p><p>One root of the equation = 7/2</p><p>Now,</p><p>4x<sup>2</sup>  -  mx + n = 0</p><p>4*(7/2)<sup>2</sup>  -  80*7/2 + n = 0</p><p>49  -  280 + n = 0</p><p>n = 231</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A working alone can take 8 hours more than B can take to complete the same work, working alone. Working together they can complete the task in 7 hours and 30 minutes. Find the time taken by A working alone to do 50% of the work.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; A &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 50% &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18 hours", "12 hours", "10 hours", "16 hours"], "options_hi": ["18 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "16 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=226 height=53 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23180/image001.png\" ></p><p>Total work = time taken by A * time taken by B = t (t  -  8)</p><p>Time = total work/ total efficiency</p><p>7.5 = t (t  -  8)/ 2t  -  8</p><p>15t  -  60 = t<sup>2</sup>  -  8t</p><p>t<sup>2</sup>  -  23t + 60 = 0</p><p>t = 20, 3 [3 is not possible]</p><p>The total work = 20 * 12</p><p>Time taken by A to do 50% of the work = 20 * 6/ 12 = 10 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=226 height=53 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23180/image001.png\" ></p><p>Total work = time taken by A * time taken by B = t (t  -  8)</p><p>Time = total work/ total efficiency</p><p>7.5 = t (t  -  8)/ 2t  -  8</p><p>15t  -  60 = t<sup>2</sup>  -  8t</p><p>t<sup>2</sup>  -  23t + 60 = 0</p><p>t = 20, 3 [3 is not possible]</p><p>The total work = 20 * 12</p><p>Time taken by A to do 50% of the work = 20 * 6/ 12 = 10 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;The value of 8 -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">6 + 4&radic;2", "q_hi": "<p><div>8 -<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">6 + 4&radic;2", "options_en": ["2/3", "5", "4/5", "2"], "options_hi": ["2/3", "5", "4/5", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>= <img width=148 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image048.png\"></p><p>= <img width=208 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image049.png\"></p><p>=<img width=208 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image050.png\"></p><p>= <img width=148 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image051.png\"></p><p>= <img width=148 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image052.png\"></p><p>= <img width=152 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image053.png\"></p><p>= <img width=131 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image054.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= <img width=148 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image048.png\"></p><p>= <img width=208 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image049.png\"></p><p>=<img width=208 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image050.png\"></p><p>= <img width=148 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image051.png\"></p><p>= <img width=148 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image052.png\"></p><p>= <img width=152 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image053.png\"></p><p>= <img width=131 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15367/image054.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If P &#8758; Q = 15 &#8758; 16 and Q &#8758; R = 16 &#8758; 17, then (P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; P &#8758; Q = 15 &#8758; 16 &#2324;&#2352; Q &#8758; R = 16 &#8758; 17 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P) &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["33: 31: 32", "31: 32: 33", "31: 33: 32", "32: 31: 33"], "options_hi": ["33: 31: 32", "31: 32: 33", "31: 33: 32", "32: 31: 33"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Given P: Q = 15: 16, Q: R = 16: 17</p><p>So, P: Q: R = 15: 16: 17</p><p>Now,</p><p>(P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P)</p><p>= (15 + 16): (16 + 17): (17 + 15)</p><p>= 31: 33: 32</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given P: Q = 15: 16, Q: R = 16: 17</p><p>So, P: Q: R = 15: 16: 17</p><p>Now,</p><p>(P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P)</p><p>= (15 + 16): (16 + 17): (17 + 15)</p><p>= 31: 33: 32</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the area (in sq. cm) of the sector of a circle whose arc length and radius are 19 cm and 10 cm.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 19 cm &#2324;&#2352; 10 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["85", "105", "95", "75"], "options_hi": ["85", "105", "95", "75"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Area of sector = (1/2) * radius * arc length</p><p>= (1/2) * 10 * 19</p><p>= 95 sq. cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of sector = (1/2) * radius * arc length</p><p>= (1/2) * 10 * 19</p><p>= 95 sq. cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A drone is flying at an altitude of 250 meters above a lake. From the drone's position, the angles of depression to two opposite points on either side of the lake are 30&deg; and &#952;, respectively. If the width of the lake (the horizontal distance between these two points) is 900 meters, then find the distance from one point to the altitude of the flying drone where the angle of depression is &#952;. (use &radic;3 = 1.7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2344; &#2333;&#2368;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; 250 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2333;&#2368;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2309;&#2357;&#2344;&#2350;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 30&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#952; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2333;&#2368;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; (&#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2376;&#2340;&#2367;&#2332; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368;) 900 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2309;&#2357;&#2344;&#2350;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#952; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; (&radic;3 = 1.7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)</p>", "options_en": ["475 m", "425 m", "525 m", "572 m"], "options_hi": ["475 &#2350;&#2368;", "425 &#2350;&#2368;", "525 &#2350;&#2368;", "572 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the distance from one point to the altitude of the flying drone be 'X' m (the angle of depression at this point is &#952;)</p><p>The distance from another point = (900  -  X) m (angle of depression at this point is 30&deg;)</p><p>Tan 30&deg; = 250/(900  -  X)</p><p>1/&radic;3 = 250/(900  -  X)</p><p>900  -  X = 250&radic;3</p><p>X = 900  -  250&radic;3</p><p>X = 50 (18 - 5&radic;3)</p><p>X = 475 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the distance from one point to the altitude of the flying drone be 'X' m (the angle of depression at this point is &#952;)</p><p>The distance from another point = (900  -  X) m (angle of depression at this point is 30&deg;)</p><p>Tan 30&deg; = 250/(900  -  X)</p><p>1/&radic;3 = 250/(900  -  X)</p><p>900  -  X = 250&radic;3</p><p>X = 900  -  250&radic;3</p><p>X = 50 (18 - 5&radic;3)</p><p>X = 475 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The simple interest on a sum of money at 10% per annum for 2 years is &#8377;8,100. What would be the compound interest (in &#8377;) on the same sum for the same period at 15% p.a, when the interest is compounded yearly? (nearest to &#8377; 1)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 10% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#8377;8,100 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 15% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;? (&#8377;1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350;)</p>", "options_en": ["13,061", "8,100", "14,671", "12,751"], "options_hi": ["13,061", "8,100", "14,671", "12,751"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the sum = P</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>(P * 2 * 10)/100 = 8100</p><p>P = &#8377;40500</p><p>Let compound interest amount = 'C'</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>= 40500 * (1 + 15/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  40500</p><p>= 53561.25  -  40500</p><p>= &#8377;13061.25</p><p>= &#8377;13061</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the sum = P</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>(P * 2 * 10)/100 = 8100</p><p>P = &#8377;40500</p><p>Let compound interest amount = 'C'</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>= 40500 * (1 + 15/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  40500</p><p>= 53561.25  -  40500</p><p>= &#8377;13061.25</p><p>= &#8377;13061</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A spherical box has surface area 528 cm<sup>2</sup>. Find the radius of the spherical box.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 528 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;37 cm", "&radic;42 cm", "&radic;29 cm", "&radic;35 cm"], "options_hi": ["&radic;37 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "&radic;42 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "&radic;29 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "&radic;35 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Surface area of spherical box = 528 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>4 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup> = 528</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 528*7/88</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 42</p><p>r = &radic;42 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Surface area of spherical box = 528 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>4 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup> = 528</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 528*7/88</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 42</p><p>r = &radic;42 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two people, M and N, are running in the same direction at the speeds of 3X km/h and X km/h respectively, on a circular track of 40 km. Find the speed of M, if they meet again after 5 hours.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;, M &#2324;&#2352; N, 40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3X &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; X &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2375; 5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; M &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["12 km/h", "4 km/h", "8 km/h", "10 km/h"], "options_hi": ["12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "10 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed = 3X  -  X = 2X km/h</p><p>Distance = 40 km</p><p>Time = 40/2X</p><p>5 = 20/X</p><p>X = 4</p><p>Speed of M = 3X = 12 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed = 3X  -  X = 2X km/h</p><p>Distance = 40 km</p><p>Time = 40/2X</p><p>5 = 20/X</p><p>X = 4</p><p>Speed of M = 3X = 12 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>When a number is divided by 5, it leaves remainder 4. When the square of that numbers is divided by 5, calculate the remainder.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; 5 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; 4 &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2313;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; 5 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Assume the number to be 9</p><p>Square of 9 = 9<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 81</p><p>Remainder = 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Assume the number to be 9</p><p>Square of 9 = 9<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 81</p><p>Remainder = 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a partnership business, B's capital was 1/3 of A's capital. If after 8 months, B withdrew 1/4 of his capital and after 2 months more A withdrew 1/2 of his capital, then the profit ratio of A and B after a year will be:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, B &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 1/3 &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, B &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 1/4 &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; A &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 1/2 &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["2: 1", "4: 3", "5: 3", "3: 1"], "options_hi": ["2: 1", "4: 3", "5: 3", "3: 1"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>I = Investment </p><p>T = Time</p><p>Let A's capital be '12'</p><p><img width=334 height=50 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26954/image007.png\"></p><p>Hence, the required ratio = 3:1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>I = Investment </p><p>T = Time</p><p>Let A's capital be '12'</p><p><img width=334 height=50 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26954/image007.png\"></p><p>Hence, the required ratio = 3:1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the length of a certain rectangle is decreased by 4 cm and breadth is increased by 2 cm, it would result in a square of the same area. What is the perimeter of the original rectangle?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 4 cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2 cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["15 cm", "24 cm", "20 cm", "10 cm"], "options_hi": ["15 cm", "24 cm", "20 cm", "10 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let length and width of the rectangle is 'l' cm and 'b' cm respectively.</p><p>Side of square = l  -  4 = b + 2</p><p>l = b + 6 ......... (1)</p><p>Area of rectangle = Area of square</p><p>lb = (l  -  4) (b + 2)</p><p>lb = lb + 2l  -  4b  -  8</p><p>l = 2b + 4 ......... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>b + 6 = 2b + 4</p><p>b = 2 and l = 8</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 2 (l + b) = 2 (8 + 2)</p><p>= 20 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let length and width of the rectangle is 'l' cm and 'b' cm respectively.</p><p>Side of square = l  -  4 = b + 2</p><p>l = b + 6 ......... (1)</p><p>Area of rectangle = Area of square</p><p>lb = (l  -  4) (b + 2)</p><p>lb = lb + 2l  -  4b  -  8</p><p>l = 2b + 4 ......... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>b + 6 = 2b + 4</p><p>b = 2 and l = 8</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 2 (l + b) = 2 (8 + 2)</p><p>= 20 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin<sup>5</sup>&theta;( 1 - 4cosec<sup>4</sup>&theta; cot<sup>4</sup>&theta;)", "q_hi": "<p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin<sup>5</sup>&theta;( 1 - 4cosec<sup>4</sup>&theta; cot<sup>4</sup>&theta;)", "options_en": ["1/sin &#952;", "sin &#952;", "cos &#952;", "tan &#952;"], "options_hi": ["1/sin &#952;", "sin &#952;", "cos &#952;", "tan &#952;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=477 height=297 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18726/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=477 height=297 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18726/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>There were 96 litres of pure milk in a container of milkman. If some quantity of pure milk is store for himself and he poured 28.8 litres of water in his container, thus the percentage of milk in his container becomes 71(3/7)%, then what is the quantity of milk (in litres) he stored for himself?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2370;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 96 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2358;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 28.8 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 71(3/7)% &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2351;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; (&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["24 litres", "12 litres", "8 litres", "10 litres"], "options_hi": ["24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "12 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "8 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "10 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let x litres of pure milk was store for himself.</p><p>The quantity of water in the mixture = 28.8 litres</p><p>percentage of milk in his container becomes = 71(3/7)% = 500/700 = 5/7</p><p>So, (96  -  x)/(28.8) = 5/2</p><p>=&gt; 96  -  x = 5/2 * 28.8</p><p>=&gt; x = 96 - 72</p><p>=&gt; x = 24</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let x litres of pure milk was store for himself.</p><p>The quantity of water in the mixture = 28.8 litres</p><p>percentage of milk in his container becomes = 71(3/7)% = 500/700 = 5/7</p><p>So, (96  -  x)/(28.8) = 5/2</p><p>=&gt; 96  -  x = 5/2 * 28.8</p><p>=&gt; x = 96 - 72</p><p>=&gt; x = 24</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A customer pays &#8377;975 in instalments. The payment is done each month &#8377;5 less than the previous month. If the first instalment is &#8377;100, how much time will be taken to pay the entire amount?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;975 &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;5 &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340; &#8377;100 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["14 months", "15 months", "27 months", "26 months"], "options_hi": ["14 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;", "15 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;", "27 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;", "26 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Installments is given as 100, 95, 90............</p><p>This forms an A.P.</p><p>S<sub>n</sub> = 975, a = 100, d = -5, n = ? </p><p>S<sub>n</sub> = n/2 [2a + (n-1)d]</p><p>975 = n/2 [2 X 100 + (n-1)(-5)]</p><p>975 = n/2 [200 - 5n + 5]</p><p>975 = n/2 [205 - 5n]</p><p>1950 = n(205 - 5n)</p><p>1950 = 205n - 5n<sup>2</sup></p><p>5n<sup>2</sup> - 205n + 1950 = 0</p><p>n<sup>2</sup> - 41n + 390 = 0</p><p>(n  -  15)(n  -  26) = 0</p><p>n = 15 or 26</p><p>when n = 15</p><p>S<sub>n</sub> = 15/2 [2 * 100 + (15  -  1)-5]</p><p>=&gt; 7.5 [200  -  70]</p><p>=&gt; 7.5 * 130 = 975(satisfy)</p><p>When n = 26</p><p>S<sub>n </sub>= 26/2 [2 * 100 + (26  -  1)-5]</p><p>=&gt; 13[200  -  120]</p><p>=&gt; 13 * 80 = 1040 (does not satisfy)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Installments is given as 100, 95, 90............</p><p>This forms an A.P.</p><p>S<sub>n</sub> = 975, a = 100, d = -5, n = ? </p><p>S<sub>n</sub> = n/2 [2a + (n-1)d]</p><p>975 = n/2 [2 X 100 + (n-1)(-5)]</p><p>975 = n/2 [200 - 5n + 5]</p><p>975 = n/2 [205 - 5n]</p><p>1950 = n(205 - 5n)</p><p>1950 = 205n - 5n<sup>2</sup></p><p>5n<sup>2</sup> - 205n + 1950 = 0</p><p>n<sup>2</sup> - 41n + 390 = 0</p><p>(n  -  15)(n  -  26) = 0</p><p>n = 15 or 26</p><p>when n = 15</p><p>S<sub>n</sub> = 15/2 [2 * 100 + (15  -  1)-5]</p><p>=&gt; 7.5 [200  -  70]</p><p>=&gt; 7.5 * 130 = 975(satisfy)</p><p>When n = 26</p><p>S<sub>n </sub>= 26/2 [2 * 100 + (26  -  1)-5]</p><p>=&gt; 13[200  -  120]</p><p>=&gt; 13 * 80 = 1040 (does not satisfy)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>In an intergalactic hover-race covering a distance of 4000 meters, Commander Samar's cruiser finishes the race while Pilot Ashutosh is still 360 meters behind. If Samar's cruising speed is 72 km/h, what is the speed of Ashutosh's hovercraft?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>4000 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;-&#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;&#2357;&#2352;-&#2352;&#2375;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2370;&#2332;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2360; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2354;&#2335; &#2310;&#2358;&#2369;&#2340;&#2379;&#2359; &#2309;&#2349;&#2368; &#2349;&#2368; 360 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2370;&#2332;&#2364;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2358;&#2369;&#2340;&#2379;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2357;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["65.52 km/h", "60.24 km/h", "68.28 km/h", "64.12 km/h"], "options_hi": ["65.52 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "60.24 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "68.28 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "64.12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Samar beats Ashutosh by 360 m in a 4000 m race, which means Ashutosh runs 3640 m in the time Samar runs 4000 m. </p><p>So, we can find Ashutosh's speed by proportionality. </p><p>The speed of Ashutosh = (4000  -  360) * 72/4000</p><p>= 65.52 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Samar beats Ashutosh by 360 m in a 4000 m race, which means Ashutosh runs 3640 m in the time Samar runs 4000 m. </p><p>So, we can find Ashutosh's speed by proportionality. </p><p>The speed of Ashutosh = (4000  -  360) * 72/4000</p><p>= 65.52 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>In an election between A and B, every fifth vote polled was marked as invalid by the machine. In the remaining votes, A wins the election with a margin of 2500 votes or 10% of the total votes polled, over B. If 90% of the invalid votes would have been in favour of B, then which of the following would have been the result of the election?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2361;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2328;&#2379;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, A, B &#2360;&#2375; 2500 &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; 10% &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 90% &#2309;&#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["B would have won by 8%", "B would have won by 3%", "A would have won by 3%", "A would have won by 8%"], "options_hi": ["B 8% &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;", "B 3% &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;", "A 3% &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;", "A 8% &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>A  -  B = 2500</p><p>10% of total votes = 2500</p><p>Total votes = 25000</p><p>Invalid = 25000/5 = 5000</p><p>Valid = 25000  -  5000 = 20000</p><p>A  -  B = 2500 ----(1)</p><p>A + B = 20000 ----(2)</p><p>From eqn(1) and eqn(2) - </p><p>A = 22500/2 = 11250</p><p>B = 11250  -  2500 = 8750 </p><p>Invalid for B = 0.9  X  5000 = 4500</p><p>Total votes of B = 8750 + 4500 = 13250 </p><p>Percentage = [(13250  -  11250)/25000]  X  100% = 8% </p><p>Hence, B would have won by 8%.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A  -  B = 2500</p><p>10% of total votes = 2500</p><p>Total votes = 25000</p><p>Invalid = 25000/5 = 5000</p><p>Valid = 25000  -  5000 = 20000</p><p>A  -  B = 2500 ----(1)</p><p>A + B = 20000 ----(2)</p><p>From eqn(1) and eqn(2) - </p><p>A = 22500/2 = 11250</p><p>B = 11250  -  2500 = 8750 </p><p>Invalid for B = 0.9  X  5000 = 4500</p><p>Total votes of B = 8750 + 4500 = 13250 </p><p>Percentage = [(13250  -  11250)/25000]  X  100% = 8% </p><p>Hence, B would have won by 8%.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}]}